    "difficulty": "Development",
    "difficultyReason": "The student must see that average speed over a round trip is total distance over total time, not the mean of the two speeds. Part (a) partly gives this away, and the later parts repeat one method. Each leg's time is found, then the times are summed and divided into 120 km. This is a little above the scaffolded two-leg average-speed task because it is not signposted, but it has no unit conversion or hidden insight.",
